# Same setup, but Bot2 has an Ornithopter (cast for free on turn 2) and blocks: Fear of Failed Tests deals its combat damage to a creature, not to a
# player (CR 510.1), so the trigger never fires and Bot1 draws nothing beyond the draw step (library 13). The unblocked scenario is the positive control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Fear of Failed Tests
Island x3
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fear of Failed Tests.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Fear of Failed Tests)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Fear of Failed Tests)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Stack.Count = 0
[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Library.Count = 13
